    "backstory": "Yulia grew up in Hjalmark, a wind-bitten university town in the northern Starkelands, where the magic is older and rougher and the winters are six months long. Her mother is an elemental surveyor who maps storm-lines across the tundra; her older sister followed the same path. Yulia was the disappointment who preferred house parties to fieldwork and got through school on charm and last-minute cramming.\n\nShe transferred to Breedhaven University in her third year, nominally to finish her Magical Engineering degree at a better-equipped college, really because her mother told her to stop embarrassing the family in Hjalmark. The Starkelands are poorer and colder than Breedhaven, and Yulia arrived in Seedblossom with two bags, a fake ID that fooled nobody, and a determination to find out what a rich country feels like from the inside.\n\nShe rents a studio above Byte & Bloom, works the occasional bar shift at the Undergrowth when rent is due, and has built a wide and shallow network of friends across every college. She takes recreational drugs the way other students take coffee: openly, often, and with strong opinions about which alchemist does the best work. The Bloom pulls at her the way it pulls at every woman, and she handles it by not handling it, by staying out late and staying close to whoever is closest.",
